# ~/.thunderbird/.chezmoiignore
#
# Tracked on purpose (the only things chezmoi owns here):
#   <profile>/prefs.js        account definitions, identities, servers, SMTP,
#                             CardDAV, calendars, chosen preferences
#   <profile>/xulstore.json   column / pane / filter layout
#   <profile>/containers.json container identities
#
# Everything else under ~/.thunderbird is per-machine runtime state.
#
# !! NEVER track the credential files. key4.db and logins.json together
# !! decrypt to real IMAP passwords and OAuth2 refresh tokens. This dotfiles
# !! repo is public, so `chezmoi add ~/.thunderbird` must never pick them up.
# !! Accounts are recreated from prefs.js and you sign in once per account.
#
# !! Patterns below are "**/"-prefixed ON PURPOSE. A bare pattern only matches
# !! directly in the directory holding this file, i.e. in ~/.thunderbird itself.
# !! Everything dangerous lives one level down in <profile>/, so without "**/"
# !! the credential rules silently never fire and `chezmoi add ~/.thunderbird`
# !! commits key4.db. Do not "tidy" the prefixes away.
# !! Verify with:
# !!   chezmoi add --dry-run -v ~/.thunderbird/<profile>/key4.db | grep -E '^diff --git|ignoring'
# !! No output (or "ignoring") means the ignore is working.

# --- credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
**/logins.json
**/logins-backup.json
**/logins.db
**/key4.db
**/cert9.db
**/pkcs11.txt
**/encrypted-openpgp-passphrase.txt
**/openpgp.sqlite

